\subsection{Preprocessing requirements}{

\code{brulee_resnet()} requires numeric predictors. Factor or categorical
predictors need to be converted to numeric values (e.g., dummy or
indicator variables) before fitting; parsnip does \emph{not} create indicator
variables for this engine, so use a recipe (or some other method) to
make them numeric.

Predictors should have the same scale. One way to achieve this is to
center and scale each so that each predictor has mean zero and a
variance of one.
}

\subsection{Case weights}{

The underlying model implementation does not allow for case weights.
}

